</h5><p>An illustrated sheet-music cover published in 1863. An ardent abolitionist whose home was a stop on the Underground Railroad, Henry Claw Work wrote a number of popular Civil War songs.</p><p class="source"><strong>Source:</strong> The Lester S. Levy Sheet Music Collection, Johns Hopkins Sheridan Libraries &amp; University Museums.
